Ladybird limits a replaced box’s intrinsic inline sizes by its
max-height, transferred through its aspect ratio. Blink does the same:
For intrinsic sizes, its CalculateInitialFragmentGeometry() sizes a
replaced box through ComputeReplacedSize() with ReplacedSizeMode::
kIgnoreInlineLengths, which applies the block-axis limits. Gecko’s
nsLayoutUtils::IntrinsicForAxis() transfers max-height through the
aspect ratio, and min-height only when that constrains something. And
WebKit’s RenderReplaced::computeReplacedLogicalWidth() calls its
computeIntrinsicSizesConstrainedByTransferredMinMaxSizes().
